{"skill":{"slug":"comfyui","displayName":"ComfyUI"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1770278426321,"changelog":"Weight downloads with pget, install-if-missing; server install instructions","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","size":1608,"sha256":"f9abf49996c276fb1c0bb380056349350800af73989d6b7b97073e9945003118","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":1751,"sha256":"3456c30971a153a0726e3ca2ed0d71f6ea9b86dd9b2ce7cc7928f5b5f48d8792","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7923,"sha256":"1ac7844a8216dc8d89c10325301a9a69cfde5eebc00e780c89624b9f70f5f993","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/default-workflow.json","size":2887,"sha256":"78d1894b0916e87896442759285bf4340e130e3655bc495fdba3d447dc8b4fbd","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"assets/tmp-workflow.json","size":2848,"sha256":"8bbd9aae11ee699eedbd639ad701d6484acf77d7584fd8e2b0df7a99e1f9f14a","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/comfyui_run.py","size":2337,"sha256":"d3b76b83dbb60f47ffa561eaf914a69710ca475c38f492c172e2580f5b010682","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/download_weights.py","size":8305,"sha256":"238924cc6a73327222fd2b888356a082ce7c369c93d7b74a97dfa82b8069f0b8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2454,"sha256":"5376fd305a65b99fb97104329aacef3c6778c50cf7f588cf26d60b87e586c33b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789034388469,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c4329fc7d60390d2c4c540e6ee3f805b5c774e8c2e1370b4035f8ba2135fa8da","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c4329fc7d60390d2c4c540e6ee3f805b5c774e8c2e1370b4035f8ba2135fa8da","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: comfyui\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to the `scripts/download_weights.py` file. This script attempts to download and install the `pget` binary from a remote GitHub release URL (`https://github.com/replicate/pget/releases/latest/download/pget_{sysname}_{machine}`) to `~/.local/bin` if it's not already present, and then executes it. While this functionality is explicitly described in `SKILL.md` and intended for legitimate parallel downloads of model weights, the capability to download and execute a remote binary represents a significant supply chain risk and broad permission, even if the immediate intent is not malicious. The `assets/tmp-workflow.json` also contains a sensitive prompt, though the agent is instructed to edit workflows based on user input, not to exfiltrate this data.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161486529},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":12,"checkedAt":1789034388469},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This ComfyUI skill has a coherent image-workflow purpose, but it needs Review because it can automatically install and run unverified external software and accepts arbitrary model URLs with unsafe file and network handling.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The workflow runner talks to localhost ComfyUI as expected, but the weight downloader accepts arbitrary URLs and derives destination filenames unsafely, supporting the static-scan concerns about SSRF/local-resource retrieval and encoded path traversal outside the intended models directory.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill tells the agent to clone and install ComfyUI from an unpinned upstream branch, and download_weights.py installs pget from a mutable GitHub latest URL into ~/.local/bin without integrity verification before executing it.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The read_when rules include generic image-description requests, and the download instructions do not require explicit confirmation, trusted URL sources, size limits, hash checks, or path confinement before network and filesystem actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates persistent changes under ~/ComfyUI, can persist an executable pget in ~/.local/bin, can overwrite model files with --overwrite, and suggests a reusable tmp-workflow.json under skill assets that may retain user-derived prompts across runs.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Running local ComfyUI workflows is coherent with the skill purpose, and model weights are related to that use case, but the artifact also broadens ordinary image-generation prompts into a tool that can install software, download remote files, and write into a user's ComfyUI tree.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. Use it only if you trust the ComfyUI environment and the model URLs, avoid untrusted workflow JSON or pasted URL lists, prefer --no-pget unless pget is already installed from a trusted source, and pin/verify ComfyUI and model downloads where possible.","findings":"[RA1] expected: The CONTRIBUTING.md update guidance is maintainer documentation, not runtime self-modification by the skill.\n[TP4] unexpected: The artifact does disclose model downloading, but automatic unverified pget installation and broad remote file retrieval are materially overbroad for routine workflow execution.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Confirmed: download_weights.py downloads pget from a mutable latest URL, writes it to ~/.local/bin, chmods it executable, and later runs it without a pinned version or checksum.\n[RA1] expected: The --overwrite flag is a user-visible model-file replacement option, not evidence that the skill modifies its own code or configuration.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill needs local files, shell execution, and network access for its purpose, but the artifact lacks clear permission boundaries or confirmation gates for high-impact install and download actions.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Generic image-description activation is too broad for a skill that can perform installs, network downloads, local workflow edits, and persistent writes.\n[RA2] expected: Writing an edited workflow is expected for the ComfyUI runner, but using a persistent asset path without cleanup is a real privacy and stale-state concern.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Confirmed: install, dependency, model-download, and pget-install instructions are present without requiring a user-facing warning or approval step.\n[SDI-1] expected: Downloading model weights is related to ComfyUI and is disclosed in SKILL.md, but the arbitrary URL scope and automatic helper-binary behavior are under-scoped.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess call uses an argument list with shell=False, so command injection is not supported by the snippet; the main concern is execution of an unverified pget binary.\n[SQP-2] expected: README disclosure of a temp workflow file is limited, but temporary workflow editing is expected for this skill and is not independently suspicious.\n[SQP-3] expected: The default workflow prompt includes a demographic descriptor; this is a content-default concern rather than evidence of malicious or hidden behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: Confirmed: the downloader unquotes the final URL path segment after splitting and joins it to the model directory without rejecting decoded separators or traversal components, enabling writes outside the intended model subfolder.\n[T09] unexpected: Confirmed: the downloader accepts arbitrary URLs and passes them to urllib without scheme, host, redirect, or private-address validation, creating SSRF/local-resource retrieval risk.\n[T03] unexpected: Confirmed: pget is fetched from a mutable latest release URL, installed persistently, marked executable, and run without integrity verification.\n[T03] unexpected: Confirmed: fallback installation guidance clones ComfyUI and installs dependencies from unpinned upstream sources, which is purpose-related but under-controlled for normal skill activation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789034388469}}}}}